        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=4{x}^{2}-7x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (8x-7) \\\\  & =\\frac{8x-7}{2\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-7x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8x-7}{2\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-7x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & ={(\\frac{8x-7}{2\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-7x}})|}_{x=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(4)-7}{2\\sqrt{4(4{)}^{2}-7(4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
